<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<model version="NetLogo 7.0.4" snapToGrid="false">
  <code><![CDATA[
extensions [ nw resource ]

breed [ mice mouse ]
breed [ frogs frog ]

directed-link-breed [ directed-edges directed-edge ]
undirected-link-breed [ undirected-edges undirected-edge ]

turtles-own [ tvar ]
mice-own [ age fur ]
frogs-own [ age spots ]
directed-edges-own [ lvar ]
undirected-edges-own [ weight ]

to setup
  clear-all
  clear-output
  reset-ticks
end

; Loads one bundled graph per `go`, cycling through every bundled resource so each format is
; checked on its own in a freshly cleared world.  `clear-all` freshens the world but also zeroes
; the tick counter, so we grab `ticks` first, clear, then rebuild the count and tick once more --
; the same "one action per tick" save/restore ImportATest uses around its world imports.  Run
; this 15 times (one per resource) to cover every format; the docking harness compares the
; world after each `go`.
to go
  let name item ticks sort resource:list
  clear-turtles
  nw:load-from-string (format-of name) (resource:get name) turtles links
  tick
end

to load-selected
  load-graph graph-name
end

to load-all
  foreach sort resource:list [ name ->
    load-graph name
  ]
end

to load-graph [ name ]
  clear-all
  show (word "loading " name)
  nw:load-from-string (format-of name) (resource:get name) turtles links
  if circle-layout? [
    layout-circle sort turtles (min (list (world-width / 2 - 2) (world-height / 2 - 2)))
  ]
  output-print (word name ": " count turtles " turtles, " count links " links")
end

; Every resource is named "<format>-<file>", so the format a file is in can be
; recovered from the resource name itself.
to-report format-of [ name ]
  report substring name 0 position "-" name
end
]]></code>
  <widgets>
    <view x="285" y="10" width="429" height="429" minPxcor="-16" maxPxcor="16" minPycor="-16" maxPycor="16" patchSize="13.0" wrappingAllowedX="true" wrappingAllowedY="true" fontSize="10" updateMode="0" showTickCounter="true" frameRate="30.0" tickCounterLabel="ticks"></view>
    <button x="10" y="10" width="125" height="33" forever="false" kind="Observer" disableUntilTicks="false" display="setup">setup</button>
    <chooser x="10" y="55" width="265" height="45" variable="graph-name" display="graph-name" current="0">
      <choice type="string" value="graphml-exclude-dangling-link"></choice>
      <choice type="string" value="graphml-missing-attr"></choice>
      <choice type="string" value="graphml-missing-attr-name"></choice>
      <choice type="string" value="graphml-missing-attr-type"></choice>
      <choice type="string" value="gdf-breeds-own"></choice>
      <choice type="string" value="gdf-builtins"></choice>
      <choice type="string" value="gdf-full"></choice>
      <choice type="string" value="gdf-link-breeds"></choice>
      <choice type="string" value="gdf-missing-attr"></choice>
      <choice type="string" value="gdf-simple"></choice>
      <choice type="string" value="gdf-simple-dir"></choice>
      <choice type="string" value="gdf-simple-undir"></choice>
      <choice type="string" value="gexf-full"></choice>
      <choice type="string" value="gml-full"></choice>
      <choice type="string" value="vna-full"></choice>
    </chooser>
    <switch x="10" y="110" width="265" height="33" variable="circle-layout?" display="circle-layout?" on="true"></switch>
    <button x="10" y="155" width="125" height="33" forever="false" kind="Observer" disableUntilTicks="false" display="load selected">load-selected</button>
    <button x="150" y="155" width="125" height="33" forever="false" kind="Observer" disableUntilTicks="false" display="load all">load-all</button>
    <monitor x="10" y="200" width="125" height="50" precision="17" fontSize="11" display="turtles">count turtles</monitor>
    <monitor x="150" y="200" width="125" height="50" precision="17" fontSize="11" display="links">count links</monitor>
    <output x="10" y="260" width="265" height="179" fontSize="12"></output>
  </widgets>
  <info><![CDATA[
## WHAT IS IT?

This model demonstrates loading networks that are bundled inside the model file itself, rather than read from disk. It bundles the network test files from the NW extension's `test/` directory as NetLogo 7 resources, and loads them with `nw:load-from-string`.

It covers all five importable file formats the NW extension supports for whole-graph import: GraphML, GDF, GEXF, GML, and VNA.

## HOW IT WORKS

NetLogo 7 lets a model carry arbitrary files inside its `.nlogox` file. Use "File" > "Manage Bundled Resources" to see, add, or remove them. The `resource` extension reads them back at run time:

  * `resource:list` reports the names of every bundled resource.
  * `resource:get NAME` reports the contents of one of them as a string.

The NW extension's `nw:load-*` primitives read from a file path, which bundled resources do not have. `nw:load-from-string` takes the data as a string instead, and since there is no file name to infer the format from, it takes the format as its first argument:

    nw:load-from-string "gml" (resource:get "gml-full") turtles links

Each resource here is named `<format>-<file>`: `gml-full` is `test/gml/full.gml`, `graphml-missing-attr` is `test/missing-attr.graphml`, and so on. The `format-of` reporter pulls the format back out of the name, so `load-graph` can handle any of the bundled files without a lookup table.

The breeds and agent variables declared in the Code tab match the ones the test files expect (`mice`, `frogs`, `directed-edges`, `undirected-edges`, `tvar`, `fur`, `spots`, `lvar`, `weight`), so the attributes stored in the files are read into turtle and link variables on import.

## HOW TO USE IT

Pick a file from the GRAPH-NAME chooser and press LOAD SELECTED to import it. The output area reports how many turtles and links came in.

LOAD ALL walks through every bundled file in turn.

Most of these files carry no coordinates, so their turtles would all land on the origin. With CIRCLE-LAYOUT? on, turtles are arranged in a circle after loading. Turn it off to see the coordinates the file actually specifies — `gdf-builtins` is the one file here that sets `xcor` and `ycor`.

## THINGS TO NOTICE

The files named `missing-attr` are here because they exercise import edge cases: they name node or edge attributes that have no matching NetLogo variable, or leave out an attribute name or type entirely. They load anyway — unmatched attributes are ignored rather than raising an error.

`gdf-full`, `gexf-full`, `gml-full`, and `vna-full` all describe the same three-node network, so loading them one after another is a good way to see how much of it each format preserves. GML and VNA are untyped, for instance, so `tvar` comes back as the string `"true"` rather than the boolean.

## EXTENDING THE MODEL

Add a network file of your own through "File" > "Manage Bundled Resources", naming it `<format>-<something>`, and it will load with no code changes. (The GRAPH-NAME chooser is a fixed list of widget choices, so you would need to add it there too, or reach it through LOAD ALL.)

Try `nw:save-to-string`, the mirror of `nw:load-from-string`, to see any of these networks written back out in another format.

## NETLOGO FEATURES

Bundled resources (new in NetLogo 7), the `resource` extension, and `nw:load-from-string`.

## RELATED MODELS

"Giant Component - Network Extension Version" and "Small Worlds - Network Extension Version", alongside this model in the NW extension's `demo/` directory.

## CREDITS AND REFERENCES

The network files bundled here are the NW extension's own test fixtures:
https://github.com/NetLogo/NW-Extension
]]></info>
